[{:db/id -1, :app/body "# Gad (Windows AMD ROCm) Ollama + Gemma 4 26B A4B setup\n\nRun these once after the Windows host (192.168.1.22) is back online.\nGoal: move Gemma vision scoring from Mac M4 → gad's AMD Radeon GPU,\nfreeing the Mac for batch orchestration.\n\n## 1. Install Ollama on Windows (if not already)\n\nOpen PowerShell on gad and run:\n\n```powershell\n# Check if installed\nollama --version\n\n# If missing, download installer\nInvoke-WebRequest -Uri https://ollama.com/download/OllamaSetup.exe `\n                   -OutFile $env:TEMP\\OllamaSetup.exe\n& $env:TEMP\\OllamaSetup.exe\n```\n\n## 2. Enable LAN listen + AMD ROCm\n\nPowerShell as Admin:\n\n```powershell\n# Listen on all interfaces (so Mac can reach :11434)\n[System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(\"OLLAMA_HOST\",\"0.0.0.0:11434\",\"User\")\n# Force AMD ROCm/HIP backend\n[System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(\"HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION\",\"11.0.0\",\"User\")\n# Restart Ollama to pick up env\nGet-Process ollama -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force\nStart-Sleep 2\nStart-Process ollama -ArgumentList \"serve\" -WindowStyle Hidden\n```\n\n## 3. Pull Gemma 4 26B A4B (GGUF, vision-capable)\n\nBest quant for 16GB AMD VRAM: **UD-Q4_K_XL** (~14GB).\n\n```powershell\n# This downloads ~14GB model + ~500MB mmproj for vision\nollama pull hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL\n```\n\nAlternative quants if Q4_K_XL OOMs:\n- `UD-Q3_K_XL` (~10GB) — slightly lower quality\n- `MXFP4_MOE` (~10GB) — MoE-optimized FP4, often fastest\n\n## 4. Smoke test from Mac\n\nFrom the Mac (this repo dir):\n\n```bash\n# Confirm reachability\ncurl -s http://192.168.1.22:11434/api/tags | jq\n\n# 1-shot vision call\nexport OLLAMA_HOST=http://192.168.1.22:11434\nexport OLLAMA_MODEL=hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL\n.venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom lg_mangaka.jump_benchmark_qa import score_jump_benchmark\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport time\nt = time.monotonic()\ns = score_jump_benchmark(Path('/tmp/v10-p00-scored.png'), n_samples=1)\nprint(f'elapsed: {time.monotonic()-t:.1f}s')\nprint(f'total: {s.get(\\\"total\\\", \\\"?\\\")}/100')\"\n```\n\nIf reasonable latency (<15s for 1 sample), proceed.\n\n## 5. Switch batch to gad scoring\n\n```bash\nexport OLLAMA_HOST=http://192.168.1.22:11434\nexport OLLAMA_MODEL=hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL\nbash scripts/batch-render-arc01.sh 22 44\n```\n\n## Caveats\n\n- **AMD ROCm vision is shaky.** llama.cpp + AMD has improved a lot in 2026\n  but vision (mmproj) on ROCm sometimes falls back to CPU. If latency\n  is bad (>30s/call), switch back to Mac (`unset OLLAMA_HOST`).\n- **GPU contention with ComfyUI.** Gemma + SDXL both running on the same\n  Radeon may slow each other. Watch `radeontop` or Task Manager > GPU.\n- **Memory headroom.** AMD Radeon 8060S has 16GB VRAM total. ComfyUI\n  SDXL holds ~6-8GB, Gemma 4 Q4_K_XL holds ~14GB → won't fit together.\n  Need to either:\n  - Use smaller quant (UD-Q3_K_XL = 10GB), OR\n  - Run scoring SERIALLY (ComfyUI off-cycle) — already what the batch does.\n\n## Fallback: keep Gemma on Mac, just upgrade the model\n\nIf gad ROCm proves too finicky:\n\n```bash\n# On Mac\nollama pull hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL\nexport OLLAMA_MODEL=hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL\n# OLLAMA_HOST stays default (localhost)\n```\n\nThe Mac M4 has 34GB unified memory — can run Q5_K_M or Q6_K too if\nquality matters more than speed.\n"}]